Llama in Agentic AI

Suppose you're building TravelGenie-AI.

User
   │
   ▼
Travel Planner Agent
   │
   ▼
Llama
   │
   ▼
Creates travel itinerary

The agent decides what to do, while Llama provides the intelligence to generate answers, plans, or code.

====

Llama through Groq

You previously used Groq API in some of your projects.

Groq provides fast inference for models like Llama.

The flow looks like this:

Your Chatbot
      │
      ▼
Groq API
      │
      ▼
Llama Model
      │
      ▼
Response

Here:

Groq = the platform that runs the model quickly.
Llama = the AI model that understands and generates the response.

========

Easy Analogy

Imagine a restaurant:

👤 Customer → asks for food.
👨‍🍳 Chef (Llama) → cooks the food.
🍽️ Waiter (Agent) → takes the order, serves the food, and coordinates the process.
🏢 Restaurant (Groq) → provides the kitchen and equipment to help the chef work efficiently.

=======

| Term         | Meaning                                                              |
| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Llama**    | A family of AI language models developed by Meta.                    |
| **LLM**      | Large Language Model that understands and generates text.            |
| **Groq**     | A platform that runs models like Llama with very low latency.        |
| **AI Agent** | A program that uses an LLM like Llama to perform tasks autonomously. |

========
In short, Llama is the AI "brain", while tools like Groq provide a fast way to run that brain, and AI agents use it to solve real-world tasks.
